A||N||4||cscougar||Dying V-6||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||12-06-2000||09:28 AM||||My 85 v-6 has been having an intermittent miss at idle.  It runs fine at highway speeds.  The last day or two, it has been dying in drive sitting at a light with the brake on.  It starts right up and runs fine.<P>Any ideas on the intermittent miss and dying?<BR>I have replaced the IAC, Ignition module and coil.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||12-06-2000||03:52 PM||||Cougar, the closest thing I could find in the Haynes manual under trouble shooting was "Engine misses at idle" for which they list:<P>1. Spark plugs worn or not gapped properly.<BR>2. Faulty spark plug wires.<BR>3. Vacuum leaks.<BR>4. Incorrect ignition timing.<BR>5. Uneven or low compression.<P>Good luck.<P>Dave<P>86 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||12-06-2000||04:01 PM||||Also under "Engine stalls" Haynes has:<P>1. Idle speed incorrect<BR>2. Fuel filter clogged and/or water or impurities in the fuel system.<BR>3. Distributor components damp or damaged.<BR>4. Faulty emissions systems components<BR>5. Faulty or incorrectly gapped plugs.<BR>6. Faulty plug wires.<BR>7. Vacuum leaks in the fuel injection system, intake manifold or vacuum hoses.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIERO1985||12-06-2000||09:39 PM||||A good thing to check is the EGR valve and gasket if it is not recieving vacume it can miss and if it is, it may have carbon deposits on it and cause mishaps only at certain times it does not cost that much so if you have not replaced it, it would be a good idea to help narrow future problems<P>Dan<BR>85 gt v6||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||12-06-2000||09:55 PM||||The dying could be associated with the trans, if its an auto.  Your torque converter lockup may not be getting unlocked and causing it to stall when the tires stop turning.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L CONVERSION IN PROGRESS --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
